doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21998618
abstract: >-
  Sinusoidal History overlays ten named long-wave cycles of history
  (Khaldun, Kondratiev, Huntington, Schlesinger Jr., Perez, Turchin's
  secular and fathers-and-sons cycles, Dalio, Strauss-Howe, Modelski) on a
  shared 1600–2050 time axis as unit-amplitude sinusoids, each pinned to
  one explicitly documented reference peak. Nine of the
  ten cycles are paired with a real long-run empirical data series for
  stress-testing. The site is an editorial comparison tool, not a forecasting
  instrument: it makes the role of calibration, theorist motivation, and
  selection effect visible by construction. Data sources are documented on
  the site's /methods page; per-source provenance is committed alongside
  each CSV. Live at https://sinusoidalhistory.com — Zenodo does not import
  the `url:` field below, so the site address is stated here to reach the
  archived record's description.
keywords:
  - long-wave theory
  - cliodynamics
  - secular cycles
  - historical cycles
  - data visualization
